    {
      "skill_id": "fr-a1-009",
      "title": "Singular articles and noun gender",
      "explanation": "Every French noun is masculine or feminine, and the article shows which. The definite article (the) is le for masculine nouns and la for feminine nouns; before a vowel or a silent h both become l': l'ami, l'école. The indefinite article (a, an) is un for masculine and une for feminine. Gender is mostly not predictable from the meaning, so learn each noun with its article: le livre, la table, un livre, une table.",
      "examples": [
        {
          "fr": "Le garçon a un chat.",
          "en": "The boy has a cat."
        },
        {
          "fr": "La femme mange une pomme.",
          "en": "The woman is eating an apple."
        },
        {
          "fr": "L'ami arrive.",
          "en": "The friend arrives."
        }
      ],
      "references": ["FEI-INV"],
